RG DS OS: the SARADC in U-Boot, to tell the RG DS from the RG DS Plus before booting.

One card serves both handhelds: the SARADC's channel 5 reads about 1.06 V on the RG DS and 1.77 V on the RG DS Plus
(BananaLinux measured both in Linux), and uboot-rgds.fragment's preboot picks the device tree by it. The Quartz64's
device tree leaves the SARADC disabled; its reference is stated here as the fixed 1.8 V both handhelds' device trees
give it (U-Boot reads vdd-microvolts, not Linux's vref-supply, and this tree's regulators are not the handhelds').
Taken from BananaLinux's uboot-patches-universal.

--- a/arch/arm/dts/rk3566-quartz64-a-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3566-quartz64-a-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -40,3 +40,8 @@
 &vcc_sd_h {
 	bootph-pre-ram;
 };
+
+&saradc {
+	vdd-microvolts = <1800000>;
+	status = "okay";
+};
